## Engineering update: closed 5 October 2026

The [course challenge's engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows)
reports that #4471 closed on 5 October. It gives two different resolutions:

- **Parser: fixed.** The update names `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  [Parser ticket](https://github.com/bacvietswiss/mega-s01e03/issues/1): closed as completed.
- **Hint: won't fix.** The booking-v3 form was retired; the hint was not repaired.
  [Hint ticket](https://github.com/bacvietswiss/mega-s01e03/issues/2): closed as not planned.

This update is newer than the 4 October KB export. The engineering panel provides a date,
not a time or time zone. These are the desk's reported outcomes; the export does not
contain the product code or deployment evidence needed to independently verify the fix
or retirement. Do not describe both tickets as fixed.

## Reports covered

The following is the historical export's classification, not current ticket status.
Its “no ticket of its own” label describes the original merge; both causes now have the
separate GitHub tickets linked above. Closed tickets still retain their report counts.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table deduplicates report IDs, filters #4471, joins tenant configuration, and runs
the supplied classifier. Tenant locale, booking-form version and channel determine the
group; browser locale and intake tags do not. Counts describe reports, not independent
incidents or unique customers. Sources: `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`,
`src/lib/data/tenants/*.json`, `src/lib/data/desk-notes.json`, and `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`.

<Callout kind="warn">
The one-day-move footnote remains inside the parser count. The engineering update does
not explain those individual symptoms. Preserve their evidence; do not infer that all
were date-order failures or independently verified fixes.
</Callout>

The desk-note IDs are `R-41202`, `R-41209`, `R-41236`, `R-41344`, and `R-41620`.
They include adjacent-day differences, a June-only pattern, an invite arriving before
booking creation, and Lisbon/Toronto displaying different days. Any recurrence needs
the intended date, event timestamp and offset, tenant/viewer time zones, channel,
form version and a reproduction before it is assigned to a known cause.

## What the history shows

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports began in April; the July merge spike includes an older backlog. It is not a
spike of newly received incidents. Incoming reports continue through the export cutoff.
The chart uses Monday-to-Sunday weeks and each timestamp's recorded calendar date,
without converting offsets into one time zone. Receipts carry `+01:00` or `+02:00`;
merge timestamps carry `+02:00`.

## Triage after closure

The [accepted replacement decision](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) and
[current triage guide](/kb/triage/dedupe) remain in effect. Preserve the original report
and check the tenant, channel, form version and symptoms. Merge only confirmed same-cause
reports. A matching subject does not establish a duplicate, and an unknown cause stays
separate. Do not merge a new failure into a closed issue without evidence that the cause
has recurred. Rebuild this page's computed views when the source export changes.

The earlier accepted decisions remain unchanged as history; this incident update records
the later engineering outcome separately.

